			<h1 class="mt-4">Quickstart</h1>
			<p>
				Follow these steps to download, set up, and run Film Tracker on your computer.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-4">1. Clone the Repository</h2>
			<p>
				First, clone the Film Tracker repository from GitHub to download the project files.
				Open a terminal and run the following command:
			</p>
			<code>git clone git@github.com:WBS-UWG/DevOps-F26-TrackFilm.git</code>

			<h2 class="mt-4">2. Navigate to the Project Folder</h2>
			<p>
				Use the terminal to navigate to the folder containing the Film Tracker project.
				If the application is inside a subfolder, navigate to that folder as well.
			</p>
			<code>cd DevOps-F26-TrackFilm/code/Film_tracker/</code>
			<br><br>
			<p>
				Make sure you are in the directory containing the project's
				<code>pom.xml</code> file before continuing.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-4">3. Run the Application</h2>
			<p>
				Once you are in the correct directory, run the following Maven command
				to start Film Tracker:
			</p>
			<code>mvn javafx:run</code>
			<br><br>
			<p>
				Maven will compile the project, resolve the required dependencies,
				and launch the JavaFX application.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-4">Requirements</h2>
			<p>Before running the application, make sure you have:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Git installed to clone the repository.</li>
				<li>A compatible Java Development Kit (JDK).</li>
				<li>Apache Maven installed and available in your terminal.</li>
				<li>An internet connection to download project dependencies if needed.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="mt-4">What it look like in image</h2>
			<img src="/images/quickstart.png" alt="Film Tracker quickstart" width="600">
			<h2 class="mt-4">Common Issues</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Command not found:</strong>
					Make sure Git, Java, and Maven are installed and available in your system's PATH.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Build errors:</strong>
					Check that you are running the command from the directory containing
					the project's <code>pom.xml</code> file.
				</li>
			</ul>

